{"step_index":1699,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:00:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T13:00:38Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T13:00:39Z\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n6:# Legacy commands use identity.img plus overlay roots. Explicit seed-* commands\r\n13:#   2) mounts the container root as overlay(Raccoon, device/upper),\r\n176:# existing subvolumes and native devices; this helper never creates either.\r\n185:        [ -d \"$path\" ] && [ ! -L \"$path\" ] && btrfs subvolume show \"$path\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || {\r\n186:            log \"$session: existing soul subvolume missing: $name\"; return 1;\r\n218:    mount -t overlay overlay \\\r\n278:    ensure_soul \"$session\" || log \"$session: soul subvolumes failed\"\r\n279:    mount_root \"$session\" || { log \"$session: root overlay failed\"; return 1; }\r\n359:    ensure_soul \"$session\" || { log \"$session: soul subvolumes failed\"; return 1; }\r\n381:# or subvolume snapshots. The seven inherited sibling subvolumes are used\r\n1057:    [ -d \"$1\" ] && [ ! -L \"$1\" ] || seed_fail \"missing or unsafe sibling subvolume: $1\"\r\n1058:    pin_show=$(btrfs subvolume show \"$1\") || seed_fail \"not a subvolume: $1\"\r\n1061:    printf '%s' \"$pin_id\" | grep -Eq '^[0-9]+$' && [ \"$pin_id\" -gt 5 ] && valid_session \"$pin_uuid\" || seed_fail \"invalid sibling subvolume identity\"\r\n1065:    # Listing at subvolid=5 includes nested members. Do not merely check that\r\n1066:    # the seven expected names exist: reject every extra or nested subvolume.\r\n1067:    subvolume_listing=$(btrfs subvolume list \"$seed_dir/volume\") || seed_fail \"cannot enumerate seed subvolumes\"\r\n1068:    actual_subvolumes=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$subvolume_listing\" | sed -n 's/^.* path //p' | LC_ALL=C sort)\r\n1069:    expected_subvolumes=$(printf '%s\\n' @ @agent_memory @agent_rules @agent_shared @agent_skills @agent_soul @agent_user | LC_ALL=C sort)\r\n1070:    [ \"$actual_subvolumes\" = \"$expected_subvolumes\" ] || seed_fail \"seed must contain exactly seven flat sibling subvolumes\"\r\n1071:    [ ! -e \"$seed_dir/volume/@persist\" ] && [ ! -L \"$seed_dir/volume/@persist\" ] || seed_fail \"old extra persistence subvolume/layout is unsupported\"\r\n1085:    ! btrfs subvolume show \"$persist_dir\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || seed_fail \"persistence must not be a subvolume\"\r\n1128:    if btrfs subvolume show \"$guest/agent\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then seed_fail \"guest agent parent must not be a subvolume\"; fi\r\n1201:    mount -t btrfs -o \"ro,subvolid=5,device=$seed_view\" \"$seed_view\" \"$seed_dir/volume\"\r\n1204:    initial_members=$(seed_layout_pins) || seed_fail \"seed lacks seven distinct sibling subvolumes\"\r\n1207:    [ \"$(btrfs property get -ts \"$seed_dir/volume/@\" ro)\" = ro=false ] || seed_fail \"seed @ must be a normal writable subvolume\"\r\n1223:    mount -t btrfs -o \"rw,subvolid=5,device=$seed_view,device=$leaf_loop\" \"$leaf_loop\" \"$seed_dir/volume\"\r\n1233:    if btrfs subvolume show \"$guest/agent\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then seed_fail \"agent parent must be ordinary directory\"; fi\r\n1307:            mount -t btrfs -o \"rw,subvolid=5,device=$seed_view,device=$leaf_loop\" \"$leaf_loop\" \"$seed_dir/volume\"\r\n"}
{"step_index":1700,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:00:39Z","input_tokens":3218,"cache_read_tokens":178482,"output_tokens":924,"thinking":"Listing subvolumes within the seed directory is crucial for verification. The script attempts to retrieve this list and then extracts the paths, sorting them for consistent comparison. A pre-defined list of expected subvolumes is constructed. The script will compare the observed subvolumes against the expected ones to validate the structure.\n\n\nVerifying the seed subvolume structure: the inspection confirms the presence of exactly seven expected subvolumes. The upgrade process uses snapshots, sends, and receives, followed by overlay mounts for the root and agent subvolumes. The overlay setup creates a read-only view of the seed layer combined with the upgrade layer, and the agent subvolumes are bound into this view.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"sudo cat /var/lib/incus/storage-pools/3tched/.provisioning/3tchedCtlChatbot.upgrade.json","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Read 3tchedCtlChatbot.upgrade.json"}}]}
